From: ArchR
Subject: [PATCH] fdrv: skip the forced DPD calibration on Tenda AIC8800DC sticks

CONFIG_FORCE_DPD_CALIB runs a digital-predistortion calibration of the
PA at every probe. On the Tenda 2604:0013 rebadge (chip_id=7 sub_id=1,
u02) that calibration kills the chip: the calib firmware upload gets no
answer from the LMAC (cmd timed-out, -110), and every command after it
fails too - continuing to aicwf_misc_ram_init_8800dc() only produces
"rf misc ram[0x10178] rd fail: -32". So surviving the failure is not
enough; the calibration must not run at all. Captured live over serial
on an R36S Soysauce, 2026-09-04.

Skip it for this vendor and fall through to the misc-ram init path,
which is exactly what the vendor tree does when it is built with
CONFIG_DPD=n (see the CONFIG_EXT_FEM_8800DCDW block in the Makefile).
The dongle then comes up without predistortion instead of not at all.
Gated on the Tenda vendor ID so native AIC dongles keep their DPD.

--- a/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_platform.c
+++ b/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_platform.c
@@ -1618,9 +1618,17 @@
                 aicwf_patch_config_8800dc(rwnx_hw);
                 #ifdef CONFIG_DPD
                 #ifdef CONFIG_FORCE_DPD_CALIB
-                if (1) {
+                if (le16_to_cpu(rwnx_hw->usbdev->udev->descriptor.idVendor) == 0x2604) {
+                    /* Tenda rebadge: the DPD calibration hangs the LMAC
+                     * and nothing works afterwards. Go straight to the
+                     * misc-ram init, as a CONFIG_DPD=n build would. */
+                    AICWFDBG(LOGINFO, "skipping dpd calib on Tenda AIC8800DC\n");
+                    ret = aicwf_misc_ram_init_8800dc(rwnx_hw);
+                    if (ret) {
+                        AICWFDBG(LOGINFO, "misc ram init fail: %d\n", ret);
+                        return ret;
+                    }
+                } else if (1) {
                     AICWFDBG(LOGINFO, "dpd calib & write\n");
                     ret = aicwf_dpd_calib_8800dc(rwnx_hw, &dpd_res);
                     if (ret) {
                         AICWFDBG(LOGINFO, "dpd calib fail: %d\n", ret);
                         return ret;
                     }
                 }
                 #else
